WEBVTT

00:00:04.713 --> 00:00:07.815
Oxford Bookworms, stage one.

00:00:07.875 --> 00:00:12.088
The Phantom of the Opera by Jennifer Bassett.

00:00:12.147 --> 00:00:19.242
Published and Copyright Oxford University Press 1994.

00:00:19.302 --> 00:00:26.706
The Opera House in Paris is a very famous and beautiful building.

00:00:26.766 --> 00:00:41.232
It is the biggest opera house in the world Work on the building began in 1861, finished in 1875 and cost 47 million francs.

00:00:41.292 --> 00:00:48.316
It has 17 floors, 10 above the ground and 7 under the ground.

00:00:48.376 --> 00:00:56.610
Behind and under the stage there are stairs and passages and many, many rooms.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:04.990
Dressing rooms for the singers and the dancers Rooms for the stage-workers, the opera dresses and shoes.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:09.594
There are more than 2,500 doors in the building.

00:01:09.654 --> 00:01:15.657
You can walk for hours and never see daylight under the Paris Opera House.

00:01:15.717 --> 00:01:22.932
And the Opera House has a ghost, a phantom, a man in black clothes.

00:01:22.992 --> 00:01:28.474
He is a body without a head, or a head without a body.

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:35.847
He has a yellow face, He has no nose, he has black holes for eyes.

00:01:35.907 --> 00:01:41.098
This is the true story of the Phantom of the Opera.

00:01:41.158 --> 00:01:50.970
It begins one day in 1880 in the Dances dressing room.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:02:01.398
Chapter 1 The Dances Quick!

00:02:01.458 --> 00:02:03.199
Close the door!

00:02:03.258 --> 00:02:04.219
It's him!"

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:10.822
Annie Sorelli ran into the dressing room, her face white.

00:02:10.882 --> 00:02:17.616
One of the girls ran and closed the door, and then they all turned to Annie Sorelli.

00:02:17.676 --> 00:02:18.827
Who?

00:02:18.887 --> 00:02:19.918
Where?

00:02:19.978 --> 00:02:21.528
What's the matter?

00:02:21.588 --> 00:02:23.230
They cried.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.590
It's the ghost!

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.112
Annie said.

00:02:27.172 --> 00:02:30.612
In the passage, I saw him.

00:02:30.672 --> 00:02:38.396
He came through the wall in front of me, and, and I saw his face.

00:02:38.456 --> 00:02:46.242
Most of the girls were afraid, but one of them, a tall girl with black hair, laughed.

00:02:46.302 --> 00:02:49.004
Po, she said.

00:02:49.064 --> 00:02:55.048
Everybody says they see the opera ghost, but there isn't really a ghost.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:58.400
You saw a shadow on the wall.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:04.594
But, She did not open the door, or look into the passage.

00:03:04.653 --> 00:03:09.776
Lots of people see him, a second girl said.

00:03:09.836 --> 00:03:15.098
Joseph bouquet saw him two days ago, don't you remember?

00:03:15.158 --> 00:03:19.410
Then all the girls began to talk at once.

00:03:19.469 --> 00:03:26.024
Joseph says the ghost is tall, and he wears a black evening coat.

00:03:26.084 --> 00:03:36.151
He has the head of a dead man, with a yellow face, and no nose, and no eyes, only black holes.

00:03:36.211 --> 00:03:41.334
Then, Little Megsury spoke for the first time.

00:03:41.394 --> 00:03:44.005
Don't talk about him.

00:03:44.065 --> 00:03:46.006
He doesn't like it.

00:03:46.066 --> 00:03:48.397
My mother told me.

00:03:48.457 --> 00:03:50.598
Your mother?

00:03:50.658 --> 00:03:53.040
The girl with black hair said.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:57.143
What does your mother know about the ghosts?

00:03:57.203 --> 00:04:01.398
She says that Joseph Bouquet is a fool.

00:04:01.457 --> 00:04:04.971
The ghost doesn't like people talking about him.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:09.294
And one day, Joseph Bouquet is going to be sorry.

00:04:09.354 --> 00:04:11.266
Very sorry.

00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:14.348
But what does your mother know?

00:04:14.408 --> 00:04:15.469
Tell us!

00:04:15.529 --> 00:04:16.930
Tell us!

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.762
All the girls cried.

00:04:19.822 --> 00:04:23.186
Oh, dear, said Meg.

00:04:23.246 --> 00:04:27.340
But please don't say a word to anyone.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:33.585
You know my mother is the doorkeeper for some of the boxes in the opera house.

00:04:33.645 --> 00:04:38.438
Well, Box 5 is the ghost's box.

00:04:38.498 --> 00:04:46.731
He watches the operas from that box and sometimes he leaves flowers for my mother.

00:04:46.791 --> 00:04:52.674
The ghost has a box and leaves flowers in it.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:56.777
Oh, Meg, your mother's telling you stories.

00:04:56.837 --> 00:04:59.649
How can the ghost have a box?

00:04:59.709 --> 00:05:01.369
It's true!

00:05:01.429 --> 00:05:03.650
It's true, I tell you!"

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.130
Meg said.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:12.422
Nobody buys tickets for Box Five, but the ghost always comes to it on Opera Nights.

00:05:12.482 --> 00:05:15.622
So somebody does come there.

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.973
Why no!

00:05:16.993 --> 00:05:22.764
The ghost comes, but there is nobody there.

00:05:22.824 --> 00:05:26.182
The dancers looked at Meg.

00:05:26.242 --> 00:05:29.419
That how does your mother know?"

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:31.500
one of them asked.

00:05:31.559 --> 00:05:37.191
There's no man in a black evening coat, with a yellow face.

00:05:37.251 --> 00:05:39.532
That's all wrong.

00:05:39.592 --> 00:05:46.324
My mother never sees the ghost in Box 5, but she hears him.

00:05:46.384 --> 00:05:51.026
He talks to her, but there is nobody there.

00:05:51.085 --> 00:05:56.255
And he doesn't like people talking about him.

00:05:56.315 --> 00:06:02.924
But that evening, the dancers could not stop talking about the opera ghost.

00:06:02.984 --> 00:06:09.656
They talked before the opera, all through the opera, and after the opera.

00:06:09.716 --> 00:06:17.028
But they talked very quietly, and they looked behind them before they spoke.

00:06:17.088 --> 00:06:22.786
When the opera finished, the girls went back to their dressing room.

00:06:22.846 --> 00:06:26.995
Suddenly, they heard somebody in the passage.

00:06:27.055 --> 00:06:31.496
And Madame Girie, Meg's mother, ran into the room.

00:06:31.556 --> 00:06:36.517
She was a fat, motherly woman, with a red, happy face.

00:06:36.577 --> 00:06:40.478
But tonight, her face was white.

00:06:40.537 --> 00:06:42.688
Oh, girls!

00:06:42.748 --> 00:06:43.998
She cried.

00:06:44.058 --> 00:06:47.159
Joseph Bouquet is dead!

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:53.062
You know he works a long way down, on the fourth floor under the stage.

00:06:53.121 --> 00:07:01.020
The other stage-workers found his dead body there an hour ago, with a rope around his neck.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.302
It's the ghost!

00:07:03.362 --> 00:07:05.093
cried Meggiri.

00:07:05.153 --> 00:07:12.119
The ghost killed him!

00:07:12.179 --> 00:07:31.133
Chapter 2 The Directors of the Opera House The Opera House was famous, and the directors of the Opera House were very important men.

00:07:31.193 --> 00:07:40.636
It was the first week of work for the two new directors, Monsieur-Arma-Morshamma and Monsieur-Fumar-Wishad.

00:07:40.696 --> 00:07:47.520
In the director's office the next day, the two men talked about Joseph Bouquet.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:55.508
It was an accident, Miss Yerama said angrily, or Bouquet killed himself.

00:07:55.568 --> 00:08:01.644
An accident killed himself, Miss Yerama said.

00:08:01.703 --> 00:08:04.726
Which story do you want, my friend?

00:08:04.786 --> 00:08:08.460
Or do you want the story of the ghost?

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.526
Don't talk to me about ghosts, Miss Yerama said.

00:08:13.585 --> 00:08:22.202
We have 1,500 people working for us in this opera house, and everybody is talking about the ghost.

00:08:22.262 --> 00:08:24.655
They are all mad.

00:08:24.714 --> 00:08:28.938
I don't want to hear about the ghost, okay?

00:08:28.998 --> 00:08:33.540
Mrs. Ferma looked at a letter on the table next to him.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.963
And what are we going to do about this letter, Armal?

00:08:38.024 --> 00:08:40.845
Do, cried Mrs. Armal.

00:08:40.905 --> 00:08:43.346
Why do nothing, of course?

00:08:43.406 --> 00:08:45.477
What can we do?"

00:08:45.537 --> 00:08:48.638
The two men read the letter again.

00:08:48.698 --> 00:08:51.150
It wasn't very long.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:54.271
To the new directors.

00:08:54.331 --> 00:09:01.144
Because you are new in the opera house, I am writing to tell you some important things.

00:09:01.204 --> 00:09:04.536
Never sell tickets for Box 5.

00:09:04.596 --> 00:09:08.680
That is my box for every opera night.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:14.177
Madame Jiri, the doorkeeper, knows all about it.

00:09:14.237 --> 00:09:19.100
Also, I need money for my work in the opera house.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:25.134
I am not expensive, and I am happy to take only 20,000 francs a month.

00:09:25.194 --> 00:09:26.785
That is all.

00:09:26.845 --> 00:09:34.510
But please remember, I can be a good friend, but a bad enemy.

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.314
Oh, gee.

00:09:37.374 --> 00:09:43.772
Don't sell tickets for Box 5, 20,000 francs a month!

00:09:43.832 --> 00:09:46.824
Mr. Omar was very angry again.

00:09:46.884 --> 00:09:51.728
That's the best box in the Opera House, and we need the money for ma.

00:09:51.788 --> 00:09:54.280
And who is this OG, eh?

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:55.962
Tell me that.

00:09:56.022 --> 00:10:01.316
Opera Ghost, of course, Mrs. Fermar said.

00:10:01.376 --> 00:10:03.998
But you're right, Omar.

00:10:04.058 --> 00:10:06.929
We can do nothing about this letter.

00:10:06.989 --> 00:10:10.320
It's a joke, a bad joke.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:15.394
Somebody thinks we are fools, because we are new here.

00:10:15.454 --> 00:10:19.727
There are no ghosts in the opera house.

00:10:19.787 --> 00:10:24.380
The two men then talked about the opera for that night.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:29.911
It was Faust, and usually, like a lot of sang margarita.

00:10:29.971 --> 00:10:34.430
La Calotta was Spanish, and the best singer in Paris.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:38.824
But today, La Calotta was ill.

00:10:38.884 --> 00:10:44.478
Everybody in Paris is going to be at the Opera tonight, said Monsieur Armand.

00:10:44.538 --> 00:10:47.980
And our best singer is ill, suddenly.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:51.042
She writes a letter to us just this morning.

00:10:51.102 --> 00:10:54.184
She is ill, she cannot sing tonight.

00:10:54.244 --> 00:10:57.656
Don't get angry again, Armand.

00:10:57.716 --> 00:11:00.110
Monsieur Fermat said quickly.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:05.552
We have Christine Daye, that young singer from Norway.

00:11:05.612 --> 00:11:08.023
She can sing Margarita tonight.

00:11:08.083 --> 00:11:10.074
She has a good voice.

00:11:10.134 --> 00:11:14.145
But she's so young, and nobody knows her.

00:11:14.205 --> 00:11:17.736
Nobody wants to listen to a new singer.

00:11:17.796 --> 00:11:20.076
Wait and see.

00:11:20.137 --> 00:11:24.218
Perhaps Daye can sing better than Larkar Lotta.

00:11:24.278 --> 00:11:30.330
Who knows?

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:36.452
CHAPTER III.

00:11:36.512 --> 00:11:39.094
CRISTINE DIAY.

00:11:39.154 --> 00:11:42.176
Ms. Thermao was right.

00:11:42.236 --> 00:11:52.262
All Paris talked about the new margarita in Faust, the girl with the beautiful voice, the girl with the voice of an angel.

00:11:52.322 --> 00:11:54.403
People loved her.

00:11:54.463 --> 00:11:58.696
They laughed and cried and cored for more.

00:11:58.756 --> 00:12:04.255
DIAY was wonderful, the best singer in the world.

00:12:04.315 --> 00:12:09.514
Behind the stage, Meg Jiri looked at Annie Sirelli.

00:12:09.574 --> 00:12:13.516
Christine Day never sang like that before.

00:12:13.576 --> 00:12:18.318
She said to Annie, why was she so good tonight?

00:12:18.378 --> 00:12:23.980
Perhaps she's got a new music teacher, Annie said.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:28.972
The noise in the opera house went on for a long time.

00:12:29.032 --> 00:12:37.042
In Box 14, Philippe, the Compt de Chani, turned to his younger brother and smiled.

00:12:37.102 --> 00:12:42.113
Well, Raul, what did you think of Diye tonight?

00:12:42.173 --> 00:12:47.454
Raul, the Viconte de Choni, was 21 years old.

00:12:47.514 --> 00:12:53.285
He had blue eyes and black hair and a wonderful smile.

00:12:53.345 --> 00:13:00.836
The Choni family was old and rich, and many girls in Paris were in love with the young Viconte.

00:13:00.896 --> 00:13:04.634
But Raulte was not interested in them.

00:13:04.694 --> 00:13:07.951
He smiled back at his brother.

00:13:08.011 --> 00:13:10.312
What can I say?

00:13:10.372 --> 00:13:13.373
Christine is an angel, that's all.

00:13:13.433 --> 00:13:16.925
I'm going to her dressing room to see her tonight.

00:13:16.984 --> 00:13:19.035
Philippe laughed.

00:13:19.095 --> 00:13:24.608
He was twenty years older than Raul, and was more like a father than a brother.

00:13:24.668 --> 00:13:29.179
Ah, I understand, he said.

00:13:29.239 --> 00:13:31.622
You are in love.

00:13:31.682 --> 00:13:37.584
But this is your first night in Paris, your first visit to the opera.

00:13:37.644 --> 00:13:41.525
How do you know Christine Daye?

00:13:41.585 --> 00:13:48.246
You remember four years ago, when I was on holiday by the sea in Brittany?

00:13:48.306 --> 00:13:49.896
Raul said.

00:13:49.956 --> 00:13:53.357
Well, I met Christine there.

00:13:53.417 --> 00:13:59.138
I was in love with her then, and I'm still in love with her today.

00:13:59.199 --> 00:14:03.582
The comp de shiny looked at his brother.

00:14:03.642 --> 00:14:08.304
Hmm, I see, he said slowly.

00:14:08.364 --> 00:14:13.288
Well, Raul, remember she is only an opera singer.

00:14:13.348 --> 00:14:16.320
We know nothing about her family.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:19.532
But Raul did not listen.

00:14:19.592 --> 00:14:28.466
To him, good families were not important, and young men never listened to their older brothers.

00:14:28.526 --> 00:14:33.978
There were many people in Christine Dyer's dressing room that night.

00:14:34.038 --> 00:14:36.870
But there was a doctor with Christine.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:40.754
And her beautiful face looked white and ill.

00:14:40.814 --> 00:14:45.387
Raoul went quickly across the room and took her hand.

00:14:45.447 --> 00:14:48.840
Christine, what's the matter?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.681
Are you ill?

00:14:50.741 --> 00:14:54.464
He went down on the floor by her chair.

00:14:54.524 --> 00:14:56.826
Don't you remember me?

00:14:56.886 --> 00:15:05.980
Raoul Darshani, in Brittany, Christine looked at him, and her blue eyes were afraid.

00:15:06.041 --> 00:15:08.712
She took her hand away.

00:15:08.772 --> 00:15:12.734
No, I don't know you.

00:15:12.794 --> 00:15:14.226
Please go away.

00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:17.058
I'm not well."

00:15:17.118 --> 00:15:21.190
Raoul stood up, his face read.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:25.243
Before he could speak, the doctor said quickly.

00:15:25.304 --> 00:15:28.716
Yes, yes, please go away.

00:15:28.776 --> 00:15:31.528
Everybody, please leave the room.

00:15:31.588 --> 00:15:34.349
Madam Azel Dayi needs to be quiet.

00:15:34.409 --> 00:15:36.980
She is very tired.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:42.493
He moved to the door, and soon everybody left the room.

00:15:42.554 --> 00:15:46.786
Christine Dayi was alone in her dressing room.

00:15:46.846 --> 00:15:53.638
Outside in the passage, the young Vee Compt was angry and unhappy.

00:15:53.698 --> 00:15:56.758
How could Christine forget him?

00:15:56.818 --> 00:15:59.829
How could she say that to him?

00:15:59.889 --> 00:16:02.320
He waited for some minutes.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:10.162
Then, very quietly and carefully, he went back to the door of her dressing room.

00:16:10.222 --> 00:16:18.435
But he did not open the door, because just then he heard a man's voice in the room.

00:16:18.495 --> 00:16:22.616
Christine, you must love me.

00:16:22.676 --> 00:16:27.731
The voice said, Then Raul heard Christine's voice.

00:16:27.791 --> 00:16:30.402
How can you talk like that?

00:16:30.462 --> 00:16:33.442
When I sing only for you.

00:16:33.502 --> 00:16:38.134
Tonight I gave everything to you, everything.

00:16:38.194 --> 00:16:41.155
And now I'm so tired."

00:16:41.215 --> 00:16:45.736
Her voice was unhappy and afraid.

00:16:45.796 --> 00:16:49.328
You sang like an angel.

00:16:49.388 --> 00:16:52.078
The man's voice said.

00:16:52.138 --> 00:16:55.088
Raul walked away.

00:16:55.148 --> 00:16:58.088
So, that was the answer.

00:16:58.148 --> 00:17:00.899
Christine Daye had a lover.

00:17:00.959 --> 00:17:04.620
But why was her voice so unhappy?

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:08.332
He waited in the shadows near her room.

00:17:08.392 --> 00:17:13.534
He wanted to see her lover, his enemy.

00:17:13.594 --> 00:17:23.388
After about ten minutes, Christine came out of her room, alone, and walked away down the passage.

00:17:23.448 --> 00:17:29.327
Raoul waited, But no man came out after her.

00:17:29.387 --> 00:17:39.299
There was nobody in the passage, so Raul went quickly up to the door of the dressing-room, opened it, and went in.

00:17:39.359 --> 00:17:45.000
He closed the door quietly behind him, then called out.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.761
Where are you?

00:17:46.821 --> 00:17:48.641
I know you're in here.

00:17:48.701 --> 00:17:50.522
Come out!

00:17:50.582 --> 00:17:53.252
There was no answer.

00:17:53.312 --> 00:17:55.734
Raul looked everywhere.

00:17:55.794 --> 00:18:02.346
under the chairs behind all the clothes in all the dark corners of the room.

00:18:02.406 --> 00:18:09.338
There was nobody there.

00:18:09.398 --> 00:18:22.882
Chapter 4 The Phantom is Angry That was Tuesday night.

00:18:22.942 --> 00:18:29.328
On Wednesday morning, Ms. Armand and Ms. Filmer were happy men.

00:18:29.388 --> 00:18:32.182
Paris liked the new Margarita.

00:18:32.242 --> 00:18:35.674
Everything in life was good.

00:18:35.734 --> 00:18:39.567
The next opera night was Friday.

00:18:39.628 --> 00:18:41.519
It was Faust again.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:46.494
But this time, with La Carlotta singing Margarita.

00:18:46.554 --> 00:18:50.828
By Wednesday afternoon, they were not so happy.

00:18:50.888 --> 00:18:56.422
A second letter arrived for them, from O.G.

00:18:56.482 --> 00:18:59.252
Why don't you listen to me?

00:18:59.272 --> 00:19:02.344
I am getting angry.

00:19:02.404 --> 00:19:05.724
Leave Box 5 free for me.

00:19:05.784 --> 00:19:09.346
And where are my 20,000 francs?

00:19:09.406 --> 00:19:14.677
On Friday, Daya must sing Margarita again.

00:19:14.737 --> 00:19:18.197
She is now the best singer in Paris.

00:19:18.257 --> 00:19:21.058
Laka Lotta cannot sing.

00:19:21.118 --> 00:19:25.670
She has a very ugly voice, like a toad.

00:19:25.731 --> 00:19:30.484
Remember, I am a bad enemy.

00:19:30.544 --> 00:19:33.206
Oh, gee.

00:19:33.266 --> 00:19:37.549
So, Therma, is this still a joke?

00:19:37.609 --> 00:19:39.970
Miss Yama, shouted.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.682
What are we going to do now, eh?

00:19:42.742 --> 00:19:46.622
Is OG the director here, or are we?

00:19:46.682 --> 00:19:52.470
Don't shout, ah, ma'am," said Mr. Fermatt, idly.

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:55.512
I don't know the answers.

00:19:55.572 --> 00:20:00.524
Let's talk to Madame Jiri, the doorkeeper of Box Five.

00:20:00.584 --> 00:20:04.216
Perhaps she can help us.

00:20:04.276 --> 00:20:08.106
But Madame Jiri was not helpful.

00:20:08.166 --> 00:20:24.066
Madame Jiri was not afraid of ghosts, and she was not afraid of directors of opera houses, People say that you're a friend of the opera ghost, Madam Jiri, Miss Yama began.

00:20:24.126 --> 00:20:26.188
Tell us about him.

00:20:26.248 --> 00:20:29.680
Some people say he has no head.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:35.546
And some people say he has no body, said Miss Yafuma.

00:20:35.606 --> 00:20:39.368
What do you say, Madam Jiri?

00:20:39.428 --> 00:20:44.524
Madam Jiri looked at the two men and laughed.

00:20:44.585 --> 00:20:50.840
I say that the directors of the opera house are fools.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:54.562
What, Missia are marshouted?

00:20:54.622 --> 00:20:58.984
He stood up, and his face was red and angry.

00:20:59.044 --> 00:21:01.125
Listen to me, woman!

00:21:01.145 --> 00:21:07.608
Oh, sit down, Arman, and listen, said Missia Fillerma.

00:21:07.668 --> 00:21:12.031
Why do you say that, Madame Jiri?

00:21:12.091 --> 00:21:18.141
Because, Missia, The opera ghost is angry with you.

00:21:18.201 --> 00:21:23.122
When the ghost wants something, he must have it.

00:21:23.182 --> 00:21:26.993
He is clever and dangerous, this ghost.

00:21:27.053 --> 00:21:33.034
The old directors before you, they knew that, oh yes.

00:21:33.095 --> 00:21:36.296
At first they tried to stop him.

00:21:36.356 --> 00:21:42.670
Then there were many accidents in the opera house, many strange accidents.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:45.603
And when did these accidents happen?

00:21:45.663 --> 00:21:48.454
When the Ghost was angry.

00:21:48.514 --> 00:21:53.566
So, the old directors learnt very quickly.

00:21:53.626 --> 00:21:56.377
The Ghost wants Fox 5?

00:21:56.437 --> 00:21:58.768
He can have it every night.

00:21:58.828 --> 00:22:01.019
The Ghost wants money?

00:22:01.079 --> 00:22:04.250
Let's give the money to him at once.

00:22:04.310 --> 00:22:10.086
Oh yes, the old directors understood very well.

00:22:10.146 --> 00:22:15.194
But we are the directors, not the opera ghost.

00:22:15.254 --> 00:22:17.686
Missia are now shouted.

00:22:17.746 --> 00:22:20.228
He turned to Missia Filmer.

00:22:20.288 --> 00:22:22.700
This woman is mad.

00:22:22.760 --> 00:22:25.183
Why do we listen to her?

00:22:25.242 --> 00:22:30.278
On Friday night, La Calotta is going to sing Margarita.

00:22:30.338 --> 00:22:37.615
And you and I, Filmer, are going to watch the opera from Box Five.

00:22:37.675 --> 00:22:45.442
Well, we can try that, Omar, but we don't want any accidents.

00:22:45.502 --> 00:22:49.676
Madam Jiri came nearer to the two men.

00:22:49.736 --> 00:22:54.440
Listen to me, she said quietly.

00:22:54.500 --> 00:22:57.452
Remember Joseph Bouquet?

00:22:57.512 --> 00:23:05.565
I tell you, the opera ghost is a good friend, but a bad enemy.

00:23:05.625 --> 00:23:09.374
The two men stared at her.

00:23:09.434 --> 00:23:15.996
Those words, Miss Yafirma said slowly.

00:23:16.056 --> 00:23:21.448
Why did you say those words, Madame Girie?

00:23:21.508 --> 00:23:25.630
Because the ghost says them to me.

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:30.562
I never see him, but I often hear him.

00:23:30.622 --> 00:23:33.716
He has a very nice voice.

00:23:33.776 --> 00:23:41.852
and he doesn't shout at people.

00:23:41.912 --> 00:23:58.178
Chapter 5 A Letter for Raul That Wednesday, a letter also arrived for the young Vikom Dushani.

00:23:58.239 --> 00:24:06.056
He opened the letter, saw the name at the bottom, and smiled for the first time that day.

00:24:06.116 --> 00:24:10.757
Dear Raul, of course I remember you.

00:24:10.817 --> 00:24:13.558
How could I forget you?

00:24:13.618 --> 00:24:20.129
Meet me on Thursday, at three o'clock, in the twillery gardens.

00:24:20.189 --> 00:24:23.610
Don't be angry with me, Raul, please.

00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:26.420
Christine Day.

00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:30.881
Raul put the letter carefully into his pocket.

00:24:30.941 --> 00:24:32.448
Angry?

00:24:32.508 --> 00:24:36.407
How could he be angry with an angel?

00:24:36.467 --> 00:24:43.122
On Thursday, he was in the twealery gardens by two o'clock.

00:24:43.182 --> 00:24:48.164
At ten past three, he began to feel unhappy.

00:24:48.224 --> 00:24:54.298
At half past three, he wanted to die or to kill somebody.

00:24:54.358 --> 00:24:58.080
And then, she came.

00:24:58.140 --> 00:25:01.342
She ran through the gardens to him.

00:25:01.402 --> 00:25:06.007
And in a second, she was in his arms.

00:25:06.067 --> 00:25:08.320
Oh, Christine!

00:25:08.380 --> 00:25:10.932
He said, again and again.

00:25:10.952 --> 00:25:14.485
Oh, Christine!

00:25:14.545 --> 00:25:21.012
They walked through the gardens together, and talked for a long time.

00:25:21.072 --> 00:25:26.874
They remembered their happy weeks in Brittany, four years ago.

00:25:26.934 --> 00:25:30.774
But why did you go away, Christine?"

00:25:30.834 --> 00:25:32.554
Raul asked.

00:25:32.614 --> 00:25:35.685
Why didn't you write to me?

00:25:35.746 --> 00:25:39.687
For a minute or two, Christine said nothing.

00:25:39.747 --> 00:25:42.788
Then she said slowly.

00:25:42.848 --> 00:25:48.140
We were so young, you and I.

00:25:48.200 --> 00:25:53.791
I was just a poor singer from Norway, and you.

00:25:53.851 --> 00:25:56.964
You were the vikom, the shiny.

00:25:57.024 --> 00:26:00.458
I knew I could never be your wife.

00:26:00.519 --> 00:26:03.860
But I love you, Christine.

00:26:03.920 --> 00:26:04.910
No.

00:26:04.970 --> 00:26:05.910
Shh.

00:26:05.971 --> 00:26:08.932
Listen to me, Raul, please.

00:26:08.992 --> 00:26:11.583
I went home to Norway.

00:26:11.643 --> 00:26:15.184
And a year later, my father died.

00:26:15.244 --> 00:26:17.568
I was very unhappy.

00:26:17.628 --> 00:26:21.572
But I came back to France, to Paris.

00:26:21.632 --> 00:26:34.142
I worked and worked at my singing, because I wanted to be an opera singer, not just a good singer, but the best opera singer in Paris.

00:26:34.202 --> 00:26:38.014
And now you are, Raoul said.

00:26:38.074 --> 00:26:39.846
He smiled.

00:26:39.906 --> 00:26:43.228
All Paris is at your feet.

00:26:43.288 --> 00:26:48.898
Christine turned her face away and said nothing.

00:26:48.958 --> 00:26:54.036
Christine, Raul said quietly.

00:26:54.096 --> 00:26:57.218
I want to ask you a question.

00:26:57.278 --> 00:27:01.609
Who was the man in your dressing room on Tuesday night?

00:27:01.669 --> 00:27:04.770
Tell me, please.

00:27:04.830 --> 00:27:08.301
Christine stopped and stared at him.

00:27:08.361 --> 00:27:11.102
Her face went white.

00:27:11.163 --> 00:27:13.233
What man?

00:27:13.293 --> 00:27:15.114
She whispered.

00:27:15.174 --> 00:27:19.637
There was no man in my dressing room on Tuesday night.

00:27:19.697 --> 00:27:23.270
Raul put his hand on her arm.

00:27:23.330 --> 00:27:26.961
I heard him, he said.

00:27:27.021 --> 00:27:32.202
I listened outside the door and heard a man's voice.

00:27:32.262 --> 00:27:34.733
Who was he?

00:27:34.793 --> 00:27:38.104
Don't ask me, Raul.

00:27:38.164 --> 00:27:40.995
There was a man's voice, yes.

00:27:41.055 --> 00:27:44.116
But there was no man in my room.

00:27:44.176 --> 00:27:45.326
It's true.

00:27:45.346 --> 00:27:49.117
Oh, Raul, I'm so afraid.

00:27:49.178 --> 00:27:52.670
Sometimes I want to die.

00:27:52.730 --> 00:27:54.760
Who is he?

00:27:54.820 --> 00:27:57.622
Tell me Christine, please.

00:27:57.682 --> 00:27:59.142
I'm your friend.

00:27:59.202 --> 00:28:00.763
I can help you.

00:28:00.823 --> 00:28:04.105
Tell me his name.

00:28:04.165 --> 00:28:07.916
I cannot tell you his name.

00:28:07.976 --> 00:28:10.188
It's a secret.

00:28:10.248 --> 00:28:12.758
Whispered Christine.

00:28:12.818 --> 00:28:14.740
I never see him.

00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:17.756
I only hear his voice.

00:28:17.816 --> 00:28:20.331
But he is everywhere.

00:28:20.391 --> 00:28:22.362
He sees everything.

00:28:22.422 --> 00:28:24.502
He is everything.

00:28:24.562 --> 00:28:28.434
That's why I didn't speak to you on Tuesday night.

00:28:28.494 --> 00:28:31.446
He is my music teacher, Owl.

00:28:31.506 --> 00:28:33.956
He's a wonderful singer.

00:28:34.016 --> 00:28:38.218
I sang so well on Tuesday night because of him.

00:28:38.278 --> 00:28:40.499
I am famous because of him.

00:28:40.519 --> 00:28:44.331
He is my angel of music.

00:28:44.391 --> 00:28:47.311
And he says he loves me.

00:28:47.371 --> 00:28:54.705
How can I leave him?

00:28:54.765 --> 00:29:11.978
Chapter 6 La Calotta Sings Margarita On Friday morning La Calotta had her breakfast in bed.

00:29:12.038 --> 00:29:16.538
She drank her coffee and opened her morning letters.

00:29:16.598 --> 00:29:19.308
One letter had no name on it.

00:29:19.368 --> 00:29:21.549
It was very short.

00:29:21.609 --> 00:29:23.720
You are ill.

00:29:23.780 --> 00:29:27.011
You cannot sing Margarita tonight.

00:29:27.071 --> 00:29:31.163
Stay at home and don't go to the opera house.

00:29:31.223 --> 00:29:33.864
Accidents can happen.

00:29:33.924 --> 00:29:36.756
Do you want to lose your voice?

00:29:36.816 --> 00:29:39.006
Forever.

00:29:39.066 --> 00:29:43.255
La Carlotta was very, very angry.

00:29:43.315 --> 00:29:47.566
She got out of bed at once and did not finish her breakfast.

00:29:47.626 --> 00:29:52.119
This is from Christine Dai's friends, she thought.

00:29:52.179 --> 00:29:55.142
They want her to sing again tonight.

00:29:55.202 --> 00:29:59.135
That Dai girl is going to be sorry for this.

00:29:59.155 --> 00:30:04.650
I, Laka Lotta, I am the best opera singer in Paris.

00:30:04.710 --> 00:30:10.812
And nothing is going to stop me singing Margarita tonight.

00:30:10.872 --> 00:30:16.643
At six o'clock that evening, the dancers were in their dressing-room.

00:30:16.703 --> 00:30:22.545
They talked and laughed, and put on their red and black dresses for Faust.

00:30:22.605 --> 00:30:26.046
But Meg-Jiri was very quiet.

00:30:26.106 --> 00:30:28.737
What's the matter, Meg?

00:30:28.797 --> 00:30:31.218
Annie Sirelli asked.

00:30:31.278 --> 00:30:35.400
It's the opera ghost, Meg said.

00:30:35.460 --> 00:30:38.301
My mother says he's angry.

00:30:38.361 --> 00:30:42.166
She's afraid that something's going to happen tonight.

00:30:42.226 --> 00:30:50.514
old poo," the girl with black hair said, who's afraid of an old ghost?

00:30:50.574 --> 00:30:59.138
An hour later, Miss your armor and Miss your filmer went into Box 5 and sat down.

00:30:59.198 --> 00:31:03.080
They were not afraid of ghosts, of course not.

00:31:03.140 --> 00:31:06.782
There were no ghosts in the opera house.

00:31:06.842 --> 00:31:13.424
Then, Miss Yama saw some flowers on the floor by the door of the box.

00:31:13.484 --> 00:31:16.865
Verma, he whispered.

00:31:16.925 --> 00:31:20.656
Did you put those flowers there?

00:31:20.716 --> 00:31:23.336
Miss Yama looked.

00:31:23.396 --> 00:31:26.247
No, I didn't.

00:31:26.307 --> 00:31:28.147
He whispered back.

00:31:28.207 --> 00:31:30.048
Did you?

00:31:30.108 --> 00:31:32.558
Of course not you fall.

00:31:32.578 --> 00:31:36.866
Shh, the music's beginning.

00:31:36.926 --> 00:31:41.134
Larkar Lotta did not sing for the first hour.

00:31:41.194 --> 00:31:47.768
There were no strange voices in Box Five, and the two directors began to feel happier.

00:31:47.828 --> 00:31:55.624
Then Larkar Lotta came out onto the stage, and Miss Yupilmaar looked at Miss Yupil Amol.

00:31:55.684 --> 00:31:59.046
Did you hear a voice just then?

00:31:59.106 --> 00:32:01.396
He asked quietly.

00:32:01.456 --> 00:32:04.994
No, Miss Yupil Amol said.

00:32:05.054 --> 00:32:13.602
But he looked behind him twice, then three times, and suddenly felt cold.

00:32:13.662 --> 00:32:19.324
La Carlotta sang and sang, and nothing happened.

00:32:19.384 --> 00:32:23.706
Then she began a beautiful love song.

00:32:23.766 --> 00:32:29.988
My love begins to quack!

00:32:30.048 --> 00:32:32.510
Everybody stared.

00:32:32.570 --> 00:32:35.700
What was the matter with Carlotta's voice?

00:32:35.760 --> 00:32:38.430
What was that strange noise?

00:32:38.490 --> 00:32:40.451
Quack!

00:32:40.511 --> 00:32:45.234
Carlotta stopped and began the song again.

00:32:45.294 --> 00:32:51.698
My love begins to quack!

00:32:51.759 --> 00:32:57.944
I cannot forget my quack!

00:32:58.004 --> 00:33:01.106
It was the noise of a toad.

00:33:01.166 --> 00:33:04.094
People began to talk and laugh.

00:33:04.154 --> 00:33:07.644
Misu Furman put his head in his hands.

00:33:07.704 --> 00:33:12.146
Then he felt Misu Omol's hand on his arm.

00:33:12.206 --> 00:33:15.748
There was a voice in the box with them.

00:33:15.808 --> 00:33:17.579
A man's voice.

00:33:17.639 --> 00:33:19.320
Laughing.

00:33:19.380 --> 00:33:22.342
Paul Carlotta tried again.

00:33:22.402 --> 00:33:23.372
And again.

00:33:23.392 --> 00:33:31.536
I cannot forget my...

00:33:31.556 --> 00:33:34.668
Then the two directors heard the voice again.

00:33:34.728 --> 00:33:40.052
behind them, in front of them, everywhere.

00:33:40.112 --> 00:33:47.868
Her singing tonight is going to bring down the chandelier.

00:33:47.928 --> 00:33:53.802
The two directors looked up at the top of the opera house.

00:33:53.862 --> 00:33:56.314
Their faces were white.

00:33:56.374 --> 00:34:06.658
The famous chandelier, with its thousand lights, broke away from its ropes, and crashed down onto the people below.

00:34:06.718 --> 00:34:11.269
That was a terrible night for the Paris Opera House.

00:34:11.330 --> 00:34:16.891
One woman was killed by the chandelier, and many people were hurt.

00:34:16.951 --> 00:34:28.283
The Opera House closed for two weeks, and La Carlotta never sang again.

00:34:28.343 --> 00:34:41.826
Chapter 7 My Angel of Music For a week Raul saw Christine every day.

00:34:41.886 --> 00:34:45.987
Some days Christine was quiet and unhappy.

00:34:46.047 --> 00:34:49.308
Some days she laughed and sang.

00:34:49.368 --> 00:34:57.881
She never wanted to talk about the opera house, or her singing, or Raul's love for her.

00:34:57.941 --> 00:35:01.744
Raul was very afraid for her.

00:35:01.804 --> 00:35:15.110
who, or what, was this strange teacher, this man's voice, her angel of music.

00:35:15.170 --> 00:35:21.321
Then, one day, there was no Christine.

00:35:21.381 --> 00:35:33.772
She was not at her home, not at the Opera House, not at their meeting places, Raul looked everywhere, and asked everybody.

00:35:33.832 --> 00:35:36.604
Where was Christine Day?

00:35:36.664 --> 00:35:39.225
But nobody knew.

00:35:39.285 --> 00:35:45.478
Two days before the Opera House opened again, a letter arrived for Raul.

00:35:45.538 --> 00:35:48.009
It was from Christine.

00:35:48.070 --> 00:35:55.558
Meet me in an hour, at the top of the Opera House, on the tenth floor.

00:35:55.618 --> 00:36:00.526
The tenth floor of the opera house was a dangerous place.

00:36:00.586 --> 00:36:04.728
There were hundreds of ropes going down to the stage below.

00:36:04.788 --> 00:36:09.442
It was a long, long way down.

00:36:09.502 --> 00:36:17.188
Raoul and Christine sat in a dark corner, and Raoul took Christine's hands.

00:36:17.248 --> 00:36:21.341
Her face was white and tired.

00:36:21.401 --> 00:36:26.400
Listen, Raoul, she said quietly.

00:36:26.460 --> 00:36:29.547
I'm going to tell you everything.

00:36:29.608 --> 00:36:32.748
But this is our last meeting.

00:36:32.808 --> 00:36:35.749
I can never see you again."

00:36:35.809 --> 00:36:37.789
No, Christine.

00:36:37.849 --> 00:36:39.420
Raul cried.

00:36:39.480 --> 00:36:41.020
I love you.

00:36:41.080 --> 00:36:43.380
And we—shh!

00:36:43.440 --> 00:36:45.111
Quietly.

00:36:45.171 --> 00:36:47.632
Perhaps he can hear us.

00:36:47.692 --> 00:36:51.182
He's everywhere in the Opera House, Raul.

00:36:51.242 --> 00:36:52.512
Who?

00:36:52.572 --> 00:36:56.482
What are you talking about, Christine?

00:36:56.542 --> 00:37:00.214
my angel of music.

00:37:00.274 --> 00:37:07.128
I couldn't meet you last Saturday because he came for me and took me away.

00:37:07.148 --> 00:37:15.744
I was in my dressing room in the opera house and suddenly he was there in front of me.

00:37:15.804 --> 00:37:19.966
I saw the voice for the first time.

00:37:20.026 --> 00:37:25.619
He wore black evening clothes and a mask over his face.

00:37:25.679 --> 00:37:33.721
He took me through many secret doors and passages, down, down under the Opera House.

00:37:33.781 --> 00:37:38.802
There is a lake down there, a big lake.

00:37:38.862 --> 00:37:43.163
The waters are black and cold.

00:37:43.223 --> 00:37:47.464
He took me across the lake in a boat to his house.

00:37:47.524 --> 00:37:54.855
He lifts their owl in a house on the lake, under the Opera House.

00:37:54.915 --> 00:37:57.924
Raul stared at her.

00:37:57.984 --> 00:38:01.666
Was his beautiful Christine mad?

00:38:01.726 --> 00:38:07.937
Christine saw his face, and said quickly, It's true, Raul!

00:38:07.997 --> 00:38:09.658
It's true!

00:38:09.718 --> 00:38:11.608
And he...

00:38:11.668 --> 00:38:15.429
He is the phantom of the opera!

00:38:15.490 --> 00:38:17.800
But he's not a ghost.

00:38:17.860 --> 00:38:20.501
He's not an angel of music.

00:38:20.561 --> 00:38:21.931
He's a man!

00:38:21.951 --> 00:38:25.090
His name is Eric.

00:38:25.150 --> 00:38:27.128
And he loves me.

00:38:27.188 --> 00:38:29.840
He wants me to be his wife.

00:38:29.900 --> 00:38:31.902
No, Raul, listen!

00:38:31.962 --> 00:38:33.744
There is more.

00:38:33.804 --> 00:38:39.628
He told me all this in his house, in a beautiful room.

00:38:39.688 --> 00:38:45.542
He said that no woman could ever love him, because of his face.

00:38:45.602 --> 00:38:48.814
He was so unhappy.

00:38:48.874 --> 00:38:56.028
Then he took off his mask, and I saw his face.

00:38:56.089 --> 00:39:02.260
She began to cry, and Raoul put his arms around her.

00:39:02.320 --> 00:39:08.032
O Raoul, he has the most terrible face.

00:39:08.092 --> 00:39:09.893
It is so ugly.

00:39:09.913 --> 00:39:14.124
I wanted to scream and run away.

00:39:14.185 --> 00:39:17.536
But where could I run too?

00:39:17.596 --> 00:39:23.998
He has the face of the dead man Raoul, but he is not dead.

00:39:24.058 --> 00:39:26.309
He has no nose.

00:39:26.369 --> 00:39:32.684
Just two black holes in his yellow face and his eyes.

00:39:32.744 --> 00:39:36.888
Sometimes they are black holes.

00:39:36.947 --> 00:39:41.712
Sometimes they have a terrible red light.

00:39:41.772 --> 00:39:45.736
She put her face in her hands for a second.

00:39:45.796 --> 00:39:52.842
Then she said, I stayed in his house for five days.

00:39:52.902 --> 00:39:55.420
He was very good to me.

00:39:55.480 --> 00:39:58.628
and I felt sorry for him, Raul.

00:39:58.688 --> 00:40:08.702
He wants me to love him, and I told him, I told him, no, Christine, no.

00:40:08.762 --> 00:40:11.393
You're going to be my wife.

00:40:11.453 --> 00:40:14.344
Come away with me at once, today.

00:40:14.364 --> 00:40:16.965
You can't go back to him."

00:40:16.985 --> 00:40:23.330
But I must, Christine said quietly.

00:40:23.390 --> 00:40:26.272
He knows about you, Raul.

00:40:26.332 --> 00:40:28.693
He knows about us.

00:40:28.753 --> 00:40:31.904
He says he's going to kill you.

00:40:31.964 --> 00:40:35.064
I must go back to him.

00:40:35.124 --> 00:40:38.195
Never said Raul.

00:40:38.255 --> 00:40:40.405
I love you, Christine.

00:40:40.465 --> 00:40:43.256
And I'm going to kill this Eric.

00:40:43.316 --> 00:40:44.156
Eric.

00:40:44.176 --> 00:40:45.076
Eric.

00:40:45.096 --> 00:40:45.356
Eric.

00:40:45.376 --> 00:40:45.886
Eric.

00:40:45.946 --> 00:40:47.187
Eric.

00:40:47.247 --> 00:40:47.807
Eric.

00:40:47.867 --> 00:40:49.458
Eric.

00:40:49.518 --> 00:40:53.778
The word whispered around the opera house.

00:40:53.838 --> 00:40:57.558
Raul and Christine stared.

00:40:57.618 --> 00:41:00.179
What was that?

00:41:00.239 --> 00:41:02.549
Raul said afraid.

00:41:02.610 --> 00:41:06.471
Was that his voice?

00:41:06.531 --> 00:41:08.521
Where did it come from?

00:41:08.542 --> 00:41:11.782
I'm afraid Raul.

00:41:11.842 --> 00:41:13.613
Christine whispered.

00:41:13.673 --> 00:41:16.964
I'm singing Margarita again on Saturday.

00:41:17.024 --> 00:41:19.475
What's going to happen?

00:41:19.535 --> 00:41:23.048
This, Raul said.

00:41:23.108 --> 00:41:28.970
After the opera on Saturday night, you and I are going away together.

00:41:29.030 --> 00:41:30.410
Come on.

00:41:30.470 --> 00:41:32.661
Let's go down now.

00:41:32.721 --> 00:41:35.681
I don't like it up here.

00:41:35.742 --> 00:41:40.513
They went carefully along a dark passage to some stairs.

00:41:40.573 --> 00:41:43.383
Then suddenly stopped.

00:41:43.443 --> 00:41:51.899
There was a man in front of them, a tall man in a long dark coat and a black hat.

00:41:51.959 --> 00:41:55.394
He turned and looked at them.

00:41:55.454 --> 00:42:01.275
No, not these stairs, he said.

00:42:01.336 --> 00:42:06.748
Go to the stairs at the front and go quickly.

00:42:06.808 --> 00:42:10.178
Christine turned and ran.

00:42:10.238 --> 00:42:12.799
Raul ran after her.

00:42:12.859 --> 00:42:14.890
Who was that man?

00:42:14.950 --> 00:42:16.260
He asked.

00:42:16.320 --> 00:42:20.100
It's the Persian, Christine answered.

00:42:20.160 --> 00:42:22.119
But who is he?

00:42:22.179 --> 00:42:23.670
What's his name?

00:42:23.730 --> 00:42:27.732
Why did he tell us to go to the front stairs?

00:42:27.792 --> 00:42:30.484
Nobody knows his name.

00:42:30.544 --> 00:42:32.765
He's just the Persian.

00:42:32.825 --> 00:42:35.456
He's always in the opera house.

00:42:35.516 --> 00:42:40.740
I think he knows about Eric, but he never talks about him.

00:42:40.800 --> 00:42:47.146
Perhaps he saw Eric on those stairs and wanted to help us.

00:42:47.206 --> 00:42:56.547
Hand in hand, they ran quickly down the stairs, through passages, then more stairs and more passages.

00:42:56.607 --> 00:43:02.472
At one of the little back doors to the opera house, they stopped.

00:43:02.532 --> 00:43:12.920
On Saturday night then, after the opera, Raul said, I'm going to take you away and marry you.

00:43:12.980 --> 00:43:16.668
Christine looked up into his face.

00:43:16.728 --> 00:43:19.272
Yes, Raul.

00:43:19.332 --> 00:43:24.893
Then they kissed, thereby the door of the Opera House.

00:43:24.954 --> 00:43:31.334
Their first kiss.

00:43:31.394 --> 00:43:41.356
Chapter 8 Where is Christine Daye?

00:43:41.417 --> 00:43:48.808
On Saturday morning, Compt Philip looked across the breakfast table at his brother.

00:43:48.868 --> 00:43:52.590
Don't do it, Raul, please.

00:43:52.650 --> 00:43:56.202
All this talk about ghosts and phantoms.

00:43:56.262 --> 00:43:58.973
I think the girl is mad.

00:43:59.034 --> 00:44:04.648
She's not mad, and I'm going to marry her, Raul said.

00:44:04.708 --> 00:44:10.110
She's only a little opera singer, Philip said unhappily.

00:44:10.170 --> 00:44:13.144
And she's very young.

00:44:13.204 --> 00:44:18.586
Are you still going to love her in 10 or 20 years time?

00:44:18.646 --> 00:44:24.148
Raoul drank his coffee and did not answer.

00:44:24.208 --> 00:44:30.251
There were two more unhappy faces in the Opera House too.

00:44:30.311 --> 00:44:34.212
The directors now understood about OG.

00:44:34.272 --> 00:44:37.683
They didn't want any more accidents.

00:44:37.744 --> 00:44:41.702
Box 5 is free tonight for OG.

00:44:41.762 --> 00:44:47.632
Dai is singing Margarita, and here is 20,000 francs.

00:44:47.692 --> 00:44:51.405
Madam Jiri can leave the money in Box Five for him.

00:44:51.465 --> 00:44:53.156
Is that everything?

00:44:53.216 --> 00:44:56.729
Miss Yama asked Miss Yefurma.

00:44:56.789 --> 00:45:02.824
It's a lot of money, Miss Yefurma said unhappily.

00:45:02.884 --> 00:45:05.156
He thought for a minute.

00:45:05.216 --> 00:45:09.286
What about some flowers in Box Five?

00:45:09.346 --> 00:45:11.655
Madame Jiri says that O.

00:45:11.715 --> 00:45:11.975
G.

00:45:12.035 --> 00:45:13.795
likes flowers.

00:45:13.855 --> 00:45:14.755
O.

00:45:14.795 --> 00:45:15.096
G.

00:45:15.156 --> 00:45:17.556
can bring his own flowers.

00:45:17.616 --> 00:45:20.027
Shouted Miss Yomor.

00:45:20.087 --> 00:45:22.928
The evening began well.

00:45:22.988 --> 00:45:27.029
The chandelier was now back in place with new ropes.

00:45:27.089 --> 00:45:29.980
All Paris was in the opera house.

00:45:30.040 --> 00:45:34.287
Everybody wanted to hear Christine Dyer's voice again.

00:45:34.347 --> 00:45:41.138
People also knew about the love story between Christine Daye and the Vikom Dushani.

00:45:41.198 --> 00:45:44.440
There are no love secrets in Paris.

00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:49.754
People watched the comp and the Vikomt in Box 14 with interest.

00:45:49.814 --> 00:45:56.750
Young men from families like Dushani do not marry opera singers.

00:45:56.810 --> 00:46:04.406
When Christine came onto the stage, her face was white and she looked afraid.

00:46:04.466 --> 00:46:07.646
But she sang like an angel.

00:46:07.706 --> 00:46:10.559
Ah, what a voice!

00:46:10.619 --> 00:46:14.532
All Paris was in love with Christine Daye.

00:46:14.592 --> 00:46:18.234
She began to sing the famous love song.

00:46:18.294 --> 00:46:23.217
Suddenly, every light in the opera house went out.

00:46:23.278 --> 00:46:27.320
For a second, nobody moved or spoke.

00:46:27.380 --> 00:46:32.896
Then, a woman screamed, and all the lights came on again.

00:46:32.956 --> 00:46:37.158
But Christine Daye was no longer on the stage.

00:46:37.218 --> 00:46:39.598
She was not behind the stage.

00:46:39.658 --> 00:46:42.149
She was not under the stage.

00:46:42.209 --> 00:46:44.820
Nobody could find her.

00:46:44.880 --> 00:46:47.760
The opera house went mad.

00:46:47.821 --> 00:46:52.502
Everybody ran here and there, shouted and called.

00:46:52.562 --> 00:46:56.723
In the director's office, people ran in and out.

00:46:56.783 --> 00:46:59.673
The police came and asked questions.

00:46:59.733 --> 00:47:02.686
But nobody could answer the questions.

00:47:02.746 --> 00:47:09.060
Mr. Armand got angry and shouted, and Mr. Furman told him to be quiet.

00:47:09.120 --> 00:47:15.032
Then Madam Jiri arrived in the office with her daughter Meg.

00:47:15.092 --> 00:47:17.623
Go away, woman!

00:47:17.683 --> 00:47:20.364
Mr. Armand shouted.

00:47:20.424 --> 00:47:25.464
Miss Yir, there are three people missing now.

00:47:25.524 --> 00:47:31.844
Madam Jiri said, Meg, tell the directors your story.

00:47:31.904 --> 00:47:35.945
This was Meg's story.

00:47:36.005 --> 00:47:41.708
When the lights went out, we were just behind the stage.

00:47:41.768 --> 00:47:43.359
We heard a scream.

00:47:43.379 --> 00:47:47.120
I think it was Christine Dyer's voice.

00:47:47.180 --> 00:47:50.122
Then the lights came back on.

00:47:50.182 --> 00:47:52.984
But Christine wasn't there.

00:47:53.044 --> 00:47:55.485
We were very afraid.

00:47:55.545 --> 00:47:58.886
And we began to run back to our dressing room.

00:47:58.946 --> 00:48:02.030
There were people running everywhere.

00:48:02.090 --> 00:48:05.954
Then we saw the viconf de chani.

00:48:06.014 --> 00:48:09.896
His face was red, and he was very angry.

00:48:09.956 --> 00:48:11.768
Where's Christine?

00:48:11.828 --> 00:48:13.288
Where's Christine?

00:48:13.348 --> 00:48:14.750
He shouted.

00:48:14.810 --> 00:48:20.763
Suddenly, the Persian came up behind him and took his arm.

00:48:20.823 --> 00:48:26.936
He said something to the viconf, and they went into Christine Dyer's dressing room.

00:48:26.996 --> 00:48:28.797
Yes.

00:48:28.858 --> 00:48:30.674
And then?

00:48:30.734 --> 00:48:35.645
Miss Yfirma said quickly, what happened next?

00:48:35.705 --> 00:48:38.217
Nobody knows.

00:48:38.278 --> 00:48:40.800
Meg's face was white.

00:48:40.860 --> 00:48:46.226
We looked into Christine Dyer's dressing room, but...

00:48:46.286 --> 00:48:53.976
but there was nobody there.

00:48:54.036 --> 00:49:08.718
Chapter 9 The House on the Lake When the lights came on, Raul ran.

00:49:08.778 --> 00:49:16.140
He ran downstairs and along passages, through the opera house to the back of the stage.

00:49:16.200 --> 00:49:23.022
In the passage outside Christine's dressing room, a hand took his arm.

00:49:23.082 --> 00:49:26.603
What's the matter, my young friend?

00:49:26.664 --> 00:49:30.306
Where are you running to so quickly?"

00:49:30.366 --> 00:49:37.750
Raul turned and saw the long face of the Persian under his black hat.

00:49:37.810 --> 00:49:41.572
Christine, Raul said quickly.

00:49:41.632 --> 00:49:43.303
Eric's got her.

00:49:43.363 --> 00:49:44.774
Where is she?

00:49:44.834 --> 00:49:46.064
Help me.

00:49:46.124 --> 00:49:49.456
How do I get to his house on the lake?

00:49:49.516 --> 00:49:53.350
Come with me, said the Persian.

00:49:53.410 --> 00:49:57.452
They went quickly into Christine's dressing room.

00:49:57.512 --> 00:50:03.716
The Persian closed the door and went to the big mirror on one wall.

00:50:03.776 --> 00:50:07.128
There's only one door into this room.

00:50:07.188 --> 00:50:08.909
Raul began.

00:50:08.969 --> 00:50:10.280
Wait.

00:50:10.340 --> 00:50:12.150
The Persian said.

00:50:12.210 --> 00:50:17.824
He put his hands on the big mirror, first here, then there.

00:50:17.884 --> 00:50:20.741
For a minute nothing happened.

00:50:20.801 --> 00:50:29.019
Then the mirror began to move and turn, and a big, dark hole opened in it.

00:50:29.079 --> 00:50:31.460
Raul stared.

00:50:31.520 --> 00:50:36.462
Quick, come with me, but be careful.

00:50:36.522 --> 00:50:40.102
The Persian said, I know Eric.

00:50:40.162 --> 00:50:42.833
I understand his secrets.

00:50:42.893 --> 00:50:49.644
Put your right hand up near your head, like this, and keep it there all the time.

00:50:49.705 --> 00:50:53.196
But why, Raul asked?

00:50:53.256 --> 00:50:58.078
Remember Joseph Bouquet, and the rope around his neck.

00:50:58.138 --> 00:51:02.940
Eric is a clever man with ropes in the dark.

00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:10.102
They went down, down, down, under the opera house.

00:51:10.162 --> 00:51:18.086
They went through secret doors in the floors, then along passages, and down dark stairs.

00:51:18.146 --> 00:51:24.350
The Persian listened carefully all the time for strange noises.

00:51:24.410 --> 00:51:27.542
When do we get to the lake?

00:51:27.602 --> 00:51:29.654
Raul whispered.

00:51:29.714 --> 00:51:32.496
We're not going by the lake.

00:51:32.556 --> 00:51:34.619
Eric watches it all the time.

00:51:34.639 --> 00:51:36.100
No.

00:51:36.160 --> 00:51:40.984
We go round the lake and get into Eric's house from the back.

00:51:41.044 --> 00:51:44.026
I know some secret doors.

00:51:44.086 --> 00:51:47.322
Soon they were there.

00:51:47.382 --> 00:51:52.678
In the dark, the Persian felt the wall carefully with his hands.

00:51:52.738 --> 00:51:53.739
Ah!

00:51:53.799 --> 00:51:55.260
Here it is!

00:51:55.320 --> 00:51:57.121
He whispered.

00:51:57.182 --> 00:52:03.106
The wall moved under his hands, and a small door opened.

00:52:03.166 --> 00:52:06.638
Very quietly, they went through.

00:52:06.698 --> 00:52:09.850
And then the door closed behind them.

00:52:09.910 --> 00:52:13.002
They could not get out.

00:52:13.062 --> 00:52:16.844
Inside the room it was very dark.

00:52:16.904 --> 00:52:19.184
They waited and listened.

00:52:19.245 --> 00:52:22.586
The Persian put his hands on the wall.

00:52:22.646 --> 00:52:24.398
Oh, no!

00:52:24.458 --> 00:52:26.000
He whispered.

00:52:26.060 --> 00:52:28.290
It was the wrong door.

00:52:28.350 --> 00:52:32.254
This is Eric's torture room, the room of mirrors.

00:52:32.314 --> 00:52:34.896
We are dead men, Vikantashani.

00:52:34.956 --> 00:52:36.957
Dead men!

00:52:37.017 --> 00:52:43.221
At first Raul did not understand, but he soon learnt.

00:52:43.282 --> 00:52:47.525
The lights came on, and they heard a man's laugh.

00:52:47.586 --> 00:52:50.648
Eric knew they were there.

00:52:50.708 --> 00:52:56.812
The room was all mirrors, walls, floor, ceiling.

00:52:56.872 --> 00:53:01.544
There were pictures in the mirrors of trees and flowers and rivers.

00:53:01.604 --> 00:53:08.058
The pictures moved and danced in front of their eyes, and the room was hot.

00:53:08.118 --> 00:53:13.440
It got hotter and hotter and hotter.

00:53:13.500 --> 00:53:22.128
Raul was thirsty, hot and thirsty and the rivers in the pictures danced and laughed at him.

00:53:22.188 --> 00:53:27.092
He closed his eyes, but the rivers still danced.

00:53:27.152 --> 00:53:28.903
Water.

00:53:28.963 --> 00:53:31.324
He needed water.

00:53:31.384 --> 00:53:34.456
But the mirrors laughed at him.

00:53:34.516 --> 00:53:41.211
Soon he could not move or speak, or open his eyes.

00:53:41.271 --> 00:53:48.376
He was not thirsty now, just tired, so tired.

00:53:48.436 --> 00:53:53.170
Oh, Christine, I'm sorry, he thought.

00:53:53.230 --> 00:53:58.813
I wanted to help you, and now I'm dying.

00:53:58.873 --> 00:54:05.478
Through a mirror in the wall, Christine watched her lover in the torture room.

00:54:05.538 --> 00:54:10.930
Behind her, Eric stood with his hands on her arms.

00:54:10.991 --> 00:54:15.614
He's dying, Christine, dying.

00:54:15.674 --> 00:54:18.046
Watch him carefully.

00:54:18.106 --> 00:54:19.094
No.

00:54:19.154 --> 00:54:21.482
Don't close your eyes.

00:54:21.542 --> 00:54:23.732
Watch him.

00:54:23.792 --> 00:54:26.592
Christine could not speak.

00:54:26.652 --> 00:54:30.813
She wanted to scream, but no words came.

00:54:30.873 --> 00:54:34.374
Ben, she found her voice again.

00:54:34.434 --> 00:54:37.355
How can you do this, Eric?

00:54:37.415 --> 00:54:40.285
Why don't you kill me?

00:54:40.345 --> 00:54:44.146
Because I love you, Christine.

00:54:44.206 --> 00:54:45.966
Marry me.

00:54:46.026 --> 00:54:49.133
Be my wife and love me.

00:54:49.193 --> 00:54:53.302
Then Raul and the version can live.

00:54:53.362 --> 00:54:57.246
Slowly, Christine turned.

00:54:57.306 --> 00:55:05.072
She looked into Eric's terrible ugly face and spoke again very quietly.

00:55:05.132 --> 00:55:07.524
Yes, Eric.

00:55:07.584 --> 00:55:12.439
For this minute, I am your wife.

00:55:12.499 --> 00:55:17.480
She put her arms around Eric's neck and kissed him.

00:55:17.540 --> 00:55:23.430
kissed him slowly and lovingly on his ugly mouth.

00:55:23.491 --> 00:55:28.813
Then she took her arms away and said slowly.

00:55:28.874 --> 00:55:33.636
Poor, unhappy Eric.

00:55:33.696 --> 00:55:36.758
Eric stared at her.

00:55:36.818 --> 00:55:41.531
You kissed me, he whispered.

00:55:41.591 --> 00:55:45.484
I didn't ask you, but you kissed me.

00:55:45.544 --> 00:55:48.396
Really?

00:55:48.456 --> 00:55:51.920
My angel.

00:55:51.980 --> 00:55:55.922
That was my first kiss from a woman.

00:55:55.982 --> 00:55:59.084
Even my mother never kissed me.

00:55:59.144 --> 00:56:04.768
She gave me my first mask when I was two years old.

00:56:04.828 --> 00:56:10.642
She turned her face away from me every time I came near her.

00:56:10.702 --> 00:56:16.186
Eric put his ugly face in his hands and cried.

00:56:16.246 --> 00:56:20.386
Then he went down on the floor at Christine's feet.

00:56:20.446 --> 00:56:23.115
You are free, Christine.

00:56:23.175 --> 00:56:24.255
Free.

00:56:24.316 --> 00:56:28.418
Go away and marry your Raul and be happy.

00:56:28.478 --> 00:56:32.210
But remember, Eric, sometimes.

00:56:32.270 --> 00:56:33.950
Go now.

00:56:34.010 --> 00:56:35.430
Quickly.

00:56:35.490 --> 00:56:43.014
Take Raul and the Persian and go.

00:56:43.074 --> 00:56:53.222
Chapter 10 Madam Jiri visits the Persian.

00:56:53.282 --> 00:56:59.274
For weeks, all Paris talked about that night at the opera.

00:56:59.334 --> 00:57:04.265
Everybody asked questions, but nobody knew the answers.

00:57:04.325 --> 00:57:07.066
Where was Christine Daye?

00:57:07.126 --> 00:57:09.917
Where was the Vikantashani?

00:57:09.977 --> 00:57:14.298
Were they alive or dead?

00:57:14.359 --> 00:57:18.810
And the Phantom of the Opera?

00:57:18.870 --> 00:57:29.296
Some weeks after that famous night, Madamjiri went out one afternoon to a small house near the rivoli gardens.

00:57:29.356 --> 00:57:34.860
She went in and up the stairs to some rooms at the top of the house.

00:57:34.920 --> 00:57:38.272
The Persian opened the door.

00:57:38.332 --> 00:57:41.743
Madamjiri looked at him.

00:57:41.804 --> 00:57:46.236
My friend, you know the answers.

00:57:46.297 --> 00:57:51.742
Please tell me, are they alive?

00:57:51.802 --> 00:57:57.046
come in," the Persian said quietly.

00:57:57.106 --> 00:58:03.842
They sat down on some chairs by the window and looked out across the riverly gardens.

00:58:03.902 --> 00:58:08.036
Yes, the Persian said slowly.

00:58:08.096 --> 00:58:11.208
The phantom is dead now.

00:58:11.268 --> 00:58:14.552
He did not want to live any longer.

00:58:14.612 --> 00:58:21.955
I saw his body three days ago, and because of that I can talk to you about him.

00:58:22.015 --> 00:58:24.756
He cannot kill me now."

00:58:24.816 --> 00:58:29.347
So, the phantom was really a man.

00:58:29.407 --> 00:58:31.867
Matamgeri asked.

00:58:31.927 --> 00:58:35.698
Yes, his name was Eric.

00:58:35.758 --> 00:58:38.948
That was not his real name, of course.

00:58:39.009 --> 00:58:43.579
He was born in France, but I knew him in Persia.

00:58:43.639 --> 00:58:48.476
He was a famous builder, and I worked with him there.

00:58:48.536 --> 00:58:54.914
For a time, I was his friend, but not for long.

00:58:54.975 --> 00:58:58.836
When he came to Paris, I came after him.

00:58:58.896 --> 00:59:01.388
I wanted to watch him.

00:59:01.448 --> 00:59:05.830
He was a very clever, very dangerous man.

00:59:05.890 --> 00:59:10.912
He could be in two or three places at the same time.

00:59:10.973 --> 00:59:16.022
He could be in one place, and his voice could come from another place.

00:59:16.082 --> 00:59:21.770
He could do many clever things with ropes and mirrors and secret doors.

00:59:21.830 --> 00:59:25.751
You see, he helped to build the opera house.

00:59:25.811 --> 00:59:31.493
He built secret passages underground and his secret house on the lake.

00:59:31.553 --> 00:59:36.854
He could not live in the outside world because of his terrible ugly face.

00:59:36.915 --> 00:59:39.206
Unhappy Eric.

00:59:39.266 --> 00:59:42.456
We can feel sorry for him, Madam Jiri.

00:59:42.516 --> 00:59:44.637
He was so clever.

00:59:44.697 --> 00:59:47.198
and so ugly.

00:59:47.258 --> 00:59:56.594
People screamed when they saw his face, and so he lived this strange life, half man, half phantom.

00:59:56.654 --> 01:00:00.447
But he was a man in the end.

01:00:00.508 --> 01:00:03.880
He wanted a woman's love.

01:00:03.940 --> 01:00:18.120
He stopped, and Madam Jiri asked quietly, and Christine Dyer, and they comped Raoul, What happened to them?

01:00:18.180 --> 01:00:21.392
The Persians smiled.

01:00:21.452 --> 01:00:23.672
Ah yes.

01:00:23.732 --> 01:00:28.574
What happened to young Raoul and the beautiful Christine?

01:00:28.634 --> 01:00:32.046
Who knows?

01:00:32.106 --> 01:00:37.798
Nobody in Paris ever saw Raoul and Christine again.

01:00:37.858 --> 01:00:44.584
Perhaps they took a train to the North and lived a quiet happy life together there.

01:00:44.644 --> 01:00:53.602
Perhaps Christine's wonderful voice is still singing, somewhere in the cold and beautiful mountains of Norway.

01:00:53.662 --> 01:00:54.885
Who knows?

